{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To find the volume of the right pyramid with a square base where each edge is 4 inches long, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Determine the side length of the square base:**\n   The side length of the square base is 4 inches.\n\n2. **Find the height of the pyramid:**\n   The height of the pyramid is the perpendicular distance from the apex to the center of the base. To find this, we need to use the Pythagorean theorem in the right triangle formed by the height of the pyramid, half the diagonal of the base, and the slant height (which is the edge length of the pyramid).\n\n   First, find the diagonal of the square base. The diagonal \\(d\\) of a square with side length \\(s\\) is given by:\n   \\[\n   d = s\\sqrt{2} = 4\\sqrt{2}\n   \\]\n   Half the diagonal is:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{d}{2} = \\frac{4\\sqrt{2}}{2} = 2\\sqrt{2}\n   \\]\n   Now, use the Pythagorean theorem in the right triangle where the height \\(h\\) of the pyramid is one leg, half the diagonal \\(2\\sqrt{2}\\) is the other leg, and the edge length (4 inches) is the hypotenuse:\n   \\[\n   h^2 + (2\\sqrt{2})^2 = 4^2\n   \\]\n   Simplify the equation:\n   \\[\n   h^2 + 8 = 16\n   \\]\n   Solve for \\(h\\):\n   \\[\n   h^2 = 8 \\implies h = \\sqrt{8} = 2\\sqrt{2} \\approx 2.828\n   \\]\n\n","prefix_end":1214,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,1477,279,8123,315,279,1290,46797,448,264,9334,2331,1380,1817,6821,374,220,19,14924,1293,11,582,1184,311,1795,1493,7354,1447,16,13,3070,35,24308,279,3108,3084,315,279,9334,2331,25,1019,256,576,3108,3084,315,279,9334,2331,374,220,19,14924,382,17,13,3070,9885,279,2608,315,279,46797,25,1019,256,576,2608,315,279,46797,374,279,76833,6010,504,279,71527,311,279,4126,315,279,2331,13,2014,1477,419,11,582,1184,311,990,279,5355,95362,45195,57817,304,279,1290,21495,14122,553,279,2608,315,279,46797,11,4279,279,37236,